                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP100904">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP100904</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1050884</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P100904</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1252920307">DTC_L3_MU_BIST</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_392746800">service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1202067456">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case 2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_128165745">Latent fault detected by BIST during startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_2109339674">No latent fault detected by BIST during startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1153342979">This DTC indicates latents fault detected during startup of the Systembasis Chip which could lead to the unavailability of its safety functions.
a.) The Logic of the Fail Safe State Machine is covered by the check "LBIST". In case of a latent fault the Fail Safe State Machine or Question / Answer Game Watchdog is not able to trigger the Fail Safe Outputs.
b.) The Fail Safe Outputs (RSTb, FS0b) and the Voltage Supervisor (VPRE, VCORE, VCCA) are covered by the check "ABIST1". In case of a latent fault, the Fail Safe Output would not be able to enter the safe state or the Voltage Supervisors are not able to detect a "out of range over / under voltage condition"
c.) The Voltage Supervisor (VAUX) is covered by the check "ABIST2". In case of an latent fault the Voltage Supervisor is not able to detect "out of range over / under voltage conditions" or an "over- / undervoltage condition is already present" which prevents the fail safe output to be released.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1009F1">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1009F1</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1051121</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P1009F1</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_370139176">DTC_L3_MU_ERR_INT</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_392746800">service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1202067456">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case 2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1620446199">Latent fault detected in SBC during run time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_991784280">No latent fault detected in SBC during runtime</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1715582740">This DTC indicates a latent fault detected during runtime of the Systembasis Chip which could lead to the unavailability of its safety functions.
a.) The Majority Voter of the triplicated structure of the Fault Error Counter of the Fail Safe State Machine is covered by the check: ERR_INT_HW
b.) Internal trim registers of the clock of the Fail Safe State Machine and the Bandgap Reference of the Voltage Supervisor are covered by the check ERR_INT_SW</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP100983">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP100983</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1051011</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P100983</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_796482306">DTC_L3_MU_SPI_COM</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_392746800">service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1202067456">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case 2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1684001589">protected SPI communication has a timeout for more than 10 ms (normal WD window, at startup 256 ms this is signalized in another DTC)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_52177121">protected SPI communication has no timeout</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1471518507"> This DTC indicates a corrupted SPI communication between the Systembasis Chip and the Microcontroller. If the watchdog of the Systembasis Chip is not refreshed properly via SPI - the Fail Safe State Machine performs a reset.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1009A1">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1009A1</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1051041</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P1009A1</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1254586128">DTC_L3_MU_LSU_CONFIG</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_392746800">service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1202067456">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case 2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1731009213">6V5Pre Configuration Check or VCCA VAUX configuration check fails</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1242177622">6V5Pre Configuration Check or VCCA VAUX configuration check passed</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_636256056">This DTC indicates a wrong HW configuration of the Voltage Regulators of the Systembasis Chip which can cause single point faults.
a.) VCCA_PNP configuration covers the current capability and the accuracy of the 5V reference for the ADC of the microcontroller. A failure causes an increased inaccuracy of ADC measurement.
b.) VCCA_HW configuration covers the supply voltage level of the 5V reference for the ADC of the Microcontroller. A failure causes an corrupted ADC measurement.
c.) VAUX_HW configuration covers the supply voltage level of analog peripherals (e.g. current sensors, rotor position sensor). A failure causes an corrupted analog measurement. 
d.) LS_DETECT configuration covers the Buck / Boost Configuration of the pre - regulator. A wrong configuration causes a limited functionality at under - voltage conditions. SBC_VPRE_CONFIG specifies the intended HW population (0... Buck only, 1.. Buck Boost)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP100956">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP100956</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1050966</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P100956</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1250253740">DTC_L3_MU_HW_CONFIG</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_392746800">service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1202067456">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case 2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1779666341">Debug Mode check fails or Deep Sleep &amp; Fail Configuration check fails</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_447833128">Debug Mode check and Deep Sleep &amp; Fail Configuration check passed</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1172697698">This DTC indicates a wrong HW configuration of the Fail Safe features of the Systembasis Chip which results in an unexpected behavior.ims to detect and react on latent faults in the HW
a.) The Debug Mode - HW Input of the Fail Safe State Machine is covered by the check: DBG_HW. In Debug Mode - the Fail Safe State Machine doesn't assert the Reset output in case of the Watchdog is not serviced properly and in addition the Fail Safe Output can not be released.
b.) The Deep Reset &amp; Fail Configuration is covered by the check DFS_HW1 and DFS_HW2. In case of the Deep Reset &amp; Fail Feature is not active, the device would not "turn Off" all voltage regulators in case of a serious HW failure.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP100955">
