                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_333429301"> This DTC indicates that the startup fail safe output check of the System Basis Chip (n Safe State Path 3) or from the MCU (Safe State Path2) has not been passed successfully. Either the output has a stuck @ low which causes a permanent shutdown of the output stages (no functionality but safe) or the output has a stuck @ high which causes a latent fault (not able to enter the safe state if required).</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1009FB">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1009FB</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1051131</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P1009FB</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2102881518">DTC_L3_MU_RSTb_CHECK</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_392746800">service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_853392376">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case 2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1600956497">open connection or short to high between SBC and MCU on Reset PIN</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1244859390">No connection problem between SBC and MCU on Reset PIN.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_840874031">This DTC indicates a failiure in the connection of the Reset between Microcontroller and Systembasis Chip.
In case of an open connection or short to high the SBC would not be able to reset the Microcontroller which is considered as latent fault.
In case of the short to low the Microcontroller is a permanent reset state and is not able to communicate to the outside world via Bus. 
A DTC is not possible, but the ECU enters the deep reset and fail and turns off all internal regulators.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_VCU.BV.BV_VCU.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1009F4">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1009F4</SHORT-NAME>
