                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_175117301">one of the HWCFG pins of the Microcontroller is not read as expected due to external pull up / pull down resistors</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1794189165">all HWCFG pins of the Microcontroller is read as expected due to external pull up / pull down resistors</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_27354874">This DTC indicates that one of the HWCFG pins of the Microcontroller is not read as expected due to external pull up / pull down resistors.
a.) HWCFG[1] failure leads to an unintended deactivation (in 5V single supply mode / activation (in 3V3 single supply mode) of the EVR33 regulator of the Microcontroller
b.) HWCFG[2] failure leads to an unintended deactivation of the EVRC (1V25) regulator
c.) HWCFG[6] failure leads to an wrong behavior of the ports in reset state (pulled high instead of tristate)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
