                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1051299</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P100AA3</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1873126202">DTC_L3_MCU_SMU_VCORE_SUPPLY_OV</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_392746800">service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1202067456">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case 2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_691848968">VCU startup</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1106516427">Voltage supervisor of the Aurix Microcontroller has detected a over voltage condition on the VDD rail out of the operating range. This common causes failure is detected during runtime.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_132069231">No Voltage supervisor of the Aurix Microcontroller has detected a over voltage condition on the VDD rail out of the operating range. No common causes failure is detected during runtime.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_752461108">Record DTC, perform safe-self reset, remain in a Safe state until ignition cycle change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1684883797">40 times clamp Cl.15_1 change</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1748257257">This DTC indicates that the voltage supervisor of the Aurix Microcontroller has detected a over voltage condition on the VDD core supply rail out of the operating range. This common causes failure which have the potential to affect several safety mechanisms is detected during runtime by the primary or secondary voltage supervisor. The safety mechanisms reports the failure to the SMUstandby which triggers a fails safe reset by the System Basis Chip. If the over voltage condition is present for a longer timespan (not just transient) the ECU enters a deep reset and fail state (internal shutdown) without DTC.
 
Note: The VDD (1V25) voltage is generated by the Aurix EVRC switching regulator istself. The VDDP3 (3V3) is in 5V single supply mode generated by the Aurix EVR33 linear regulator or supplied out of VEXT in 3V3 single supply mode.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_102334147">No INV_BUS communication, no HV activation, No Park Lock avaliabe until ignition cycle or automated
cold-restart. If ignition cycle change is not performed in 10 minutes VCU will shutdown itself. Vehicle is only able to roll out. Re-activation of HV is first possible after standstill is reached and ignition cycle change.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
